                <pb facs="0014" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.H/47: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-14T15:00:00-05:00">March 14, 1938—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. From the Under Secretary. Your 50, March 12, 11 a.m. [Here follows text of
                    first three paragraphs of telegram No. 10, March 12, 1 p.m., to the Minister in
                    Uruguay, printed <hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>In any reply you make to the Brazilian Foreign Office you may repeat in general
                    terms the views which I expressed to the Argentine Ambassador.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
